     "\r<br>\r<br>On Mon, Jan 19, 2015 at 12:20 PM, Erich Neuwirth\r<br>&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">neuwir...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I managed to get things running on Yosemite.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; I installed Qt 5.4.0 from  <a href=\"http://www.qt.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.qt.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793246423886000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1QvVZjUkaEC0z-gBLBCrPg\">http://www.qt.io</a> and Cmake 3.1.0 from\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"http://www.cmake.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.cmake.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793246423886000&amp;usg=AOvVaw36bG0Jy4Xgj6utNN2MiXyc\">http://www.cmake.org</a>.\r<br>&gt; I added the following entries to .bash_profile\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; PATH=&quot;/Users/neuwirth/Qt5.4.0/5.4/clang_64/bin:/Applications/CMake.app/Contents/bin:${PATH}&quot;\r<br>&gt; export PATH\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Then I created /opt/local/lib on the machine where it did not exist,\r<br>&gt; and on this machine and on another where it existed already, I ran\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; sudo ln -s /usr/lib/libxslt.1.dylib /opt/local/lib/libxslt.1.dylib\r<br>&gt; sudo ln -s /usr/lib/libz.1.dylib /opt/local/lib/libz.1.dylib\r<br>&gt; sudo ln -s /usr/lib/libsqlite3.0.dylib /opt/local/lib/libsqlite3.0.dylib\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Then I startet R in a terminal  window (with sudo) and than the commands in\r<br>&gt; the installation instructions,\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; only changing\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;   install_github(&#39;ggobi/qtbase@qt4&#39;);\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; to\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;   install_github(&#39;ggobi/qtbase&#39;);\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Then, I could run the examples in command line R and in RStudio.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>"
